      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It really is a pain that vrc allows people who upload a world, put effort into it and build a community, but then not be able to protect that community. There's no way to deal with bad people except box them for 1 instance. So anyone who intends to cause harm just hops to a new instance. There's also people who intentionally false ban every mod so they can cause harm without worry of being stopped.\n\nPeople report this stuff to us and our only reply is to contact vrchat. We can't protect our own community because only vrchat staff have the ability to really stop someone. While vrc does ban people saying slurs and stuff usually within 24 hours (when given a clip), the seriously bad stuff that's not just explainable in a short clip goes unpunished or they make an alt.\n\nRelated, vrc will only ban an under age user if they verbally admit they are below 13. There's loads of times where someone sounds nowhere near 13 and will never verbally admit it. Vrc just says they are \"investigating it\" but nothing ever happens.\n\nHaving the ability to actually ban people from all forms of public instances on a world would be a giant boost to the safety of the platform. Yeah there is the chance of abuse, but there are already people vetted for the creator economy, those people would likely be trustable and have a community worth protecting. Some world creators actually want to improve the platform for their community, vrchat currently doesn't let them.\n\nI also do feel that requiring a way to appeal is important. Any world owner/mods for a world over should be able to accept appeals, not everyone is perfect. Some people should be forgiven. Requiring video evidence of bans or an explanation written for the ban would also be helpful in giving the ban more weight and stopping abuse.\n\nA lot of things are just \"this person is going to be banned in a day or two, but until vrchat does that, they can just blast slurs in every instance\" or \"this is a complicated situation, everyone knows this person is super bad but vrchat isn't going to spend 30 minutes learning why and what's going on\"\n\nGiving world creators the ability to actually moderate their own worlds speeds up action and allows action too complicated for vrc themselves.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
